{"id":"1f5bff8e-37fc-42c1-aec7-aaf4cbeb376d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0118fcacc3e4c015","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"50734bbddc9768e29864ceba8f1204c5a91806c0","start":7553,"end":7594},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","embedded","=","window",".","parent","!==","window"]},"context":{"before":"205b9913e8c34b34","after":"9b33cc19805da7a0"}},"payload":{"text":"The app branch only runs inside the shell's iframe (top-level / renders the shell), so we're always embedded:\nthe editor fills the shell's middle space and links its root hub UP to the shell.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:35.328Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:35.328Z"}
{"id":"273c06e9-3cc0-4f81-b3c3-11fcbdb72b6b","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"68836a2f20628951","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"869458f250891424d8d1b047809ffab8a4dcd151","start":31,"end":89},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","{","isEditorTop",",","seedFiles","}","from","\"","./shared/instance","\""]},"context":{"after":"ff974107ecdf0280"}},"payload":{"text":"(first, before anything takes the realm's own: an instance's storage apart, a hidden tab's timers kept)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:52.471Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:52.471Z"}
{"id":"2837f84e-6744-4d24-b40e-0fa74c31b159","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"bdfa68863d345b20","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"49057ef4e6190bd1c18c2a85c88d32e038557611","start":1760,"end":1792},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["performance",".","mark","(","\"","shell/import","\"",")"]},"context":{"before":"1c35a4b67d57bcf7","after":"d3ae470645e97bed"}},"payload":{"text":"TOP LEVEL: render the outer shell — the app's main layout (chrome + RHS review panel). It\niframes THIS same page back in; that nested instance sees `window.parent !== window` and takes the app\nbranch below, booting the workbench into the middle (fill mode). One entry, one bundle, one COI bootstrap.\nDYNAMIC import so the shell's WebAwesome chrome (wa-page, wa-button, the theme) lands in a shell-only chunk and\nnever loads in the app iframe — the editor realm stays WA-free.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:49.662Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:49.662Z"}
{"id":"28bd75ef-26ed-43cb-89cc-525683730721","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"205b9913e8c34b34","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"2df55b84df6d0aa03e81ab02e2c412770cf81141","start":6978,"end":7110},"shape":{"type":"UnaryExpression","atoms":["void","import","(","\"","./app/tools","\"",")",".","then","(","(","{","editorTools","}",")","=>","{","servePageTools","(","rootHub",",","{","\"","tab","\"",":","tab",",","\"","tools","\"",":","editorTools","(","rootHub",")","}",")",";","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"6bbb3bd670093e52","after":"0118fcacc3e4c015"}},"payload":{"text":"Dev-only: this tab's MCP tools, which debug-mcp registers while it's connected — under this tab's id, so it can\naddress one tab of several: every page's page_eval / page_query, and the editor's own (the debugger, the preview's\ncold-start provoke, a preview page's Chrome DevTools Protocol — see tools/).\n(tools/: a folder per family, each util/mcp's own tools — loaded after boot, so the MCP SDK and zod stay off its path)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:36.812Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:36.812Z"}
{"id":"2f69ef19-f50c-4bed-a3d0-b3d5c209163a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"47c8076a52d06a33","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"33493c7b63daae9f9344fcbb22c05523276a2d57","start":3867,"end":3915},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","architecture","=","reportArchitecture","(","rootHub",")"]},"context":{"before":"3acaf830235d86ad","after":"2a12997a5a903f8b"}},"payload":{"text":"This realm's hub + network on $sys.arch, for the live architecture view — plus every message another frame posts\nhere that isn't hub traffic (the shell above, the workbench iframe below), so a new channel can't hide.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:45.609Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:45.609Z"}
{"id":"39f65ee9-ac5d-40e4-8e64-c8f1dc8cb5e1","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3acaf830235d86ad","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"2823d0a3f73133be11de3ccbf2fba9be94f91a7d","start":3524,"end":3567},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","rootHub","=","createHub","(","{","\"","id","\"",":","\"","root","\"","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"d65514566fc3605b","after":"47c8076a52d06a33"}},"payload":{"text":"The root hub — top of the composable-hub tree. A collector renders every context's spans/records off the\n`$sys.log.>` observability plane (the service worker now, the pod + workers next); the SW links in over a\ndedicated port. See @brianjenkins94/observability / @brianjenkins94/hub.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:46.927Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:46.927Z"}
{"id":"7ee9f42f-2ff4-4c1e-ab9b-7b233d3ed773","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"caade1ba94506e79","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"0693284d88f9f528caea612a161050bcc4c7b575","start":6353,"end":6510},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["serve","(","rootHub",",","`","capability.decide.","${","tab","}","","`",",","async","(","args",")","=>","tabRpc",".","request","(","\"","capability.decide","\"",",","args",",","{","\"","timeoutMs","\"",":","300_000",",","\"","waitForResponderMs","\"",":","10_000","}",")",")"]},"context":{"before":"25dde730b03dfa5e","after":"8743f809525d52c4"}},"payload":{"text":"A preview's outside calls, as the service worker asks: decided by the bridge (extensions/bridge/preview-gate.ts). A person\nmay be deliberating.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:38.169Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:38.169Z"}
{"id":"908c2721-2826-4534-a5f2-4e919a8ffd04","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7b9d9ed09bc1616a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"55cd6f46c1d8ec4c5807137ca1ce7043e398fefa","start":9000,"end":9069},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["vscodeWindow",".","replaceProject","(","request",".","files",",","request",".","openEditors","??","[","]",")"]},"context":{"before":"476fbf9eb67f3dbf","after":"4fc12a0cf2188a14"}},"payload":{"text":"Replace: the loaded repo becomes the workspace (clears the demo first).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:30.865Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:30.865Z"}
{"id":"93cfc065-33d6-4ccc-9a22-9440381d9e8a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a20da9deb0a24dcc","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"b4690e8e80bed98e14242d39b3cf6c1db58ad0b0","start":4434,"end":4474},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","spans","=","reportSpanMetrics","(","rootHub",")"]},"context":{"before":"2a12997a5a903f8b","after":"889da2446c181733"}},"payload":{"text":"Every context's records arrive here: to the console, and — their spans — onto the metrics plane as rates, errors and\nlatencies (editor-metrics.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:43.900Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:43.900Z"}
{"id":"a499f4f4-d196-4e7d-a3da-12a5b7a6b7ba","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6185af3308b1a3bd","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"4d891d447f3f6cabd7470de55d8a0febddc1dff9","start":908,"end":962},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","reset","=","isEditorTop","(",")","?","resetAsked","(",")",":","undefined"]},"context":{"before":"b566170ac0871cf8","after":"be1eab04ed719779"}},"payload":{"text":"Gain cross-origin isolation (SharedArrayBuffer) before booting. A dev server already sends the COOP/COEP\nheaders; on a static host (GitHub Pages) the coi service worker supplies them after one reload. On the\nun-isolated first load this returns false and schedules that reload, so we skip booting until the page\ncomes back isolated.\n`?reset` (shell/reset.ts): before any of that — the service worker and the workbench would hold what it deletes.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:51.164Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:51.164Z"}
{"id":"b1fcce3e-9378-4ce0-b0a7-242e954cc393","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"43ac3b0b31c10e62","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"2762478ae4a979cf02f5a9734c9649a3c71e6e45","start":5753,"end":5796},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","tab","=","crypto",".","randomUUID","(",")",".","slice","(","0",",","8",")"]},"context":{"before":"bf52e0eb363ec23f","after":"c1852e768376b921"}},"payload":{"text":"This tab's id: debug-mcp addresses this tab's page tools by it, apart from every other tab's.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:41.125Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:41.125Z"}
{"id":"c46cc0fe-eeb1-4079-8027-f943b9d772cb","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"c5b925ff4cc27dfc","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"e5427f3a01211653a56277b5e4630827ac4dbe3f","start":4732,"end":4867},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","attrs","=","(","record",".","attrs","??","{","}",")","as","{","\"","src","\"","?",":","unknown",";","\"","line","\"","?",":","unknown",";","\"","stack","\"","?",":","unknown",";","\"","message","\"","?",":","unknown",";","\"","reason","\"","?",":","unknown","}"]},"context":{"before":"17bbd0565c1efa3d","after":"c6b55066237d6dee"}},"payload":{"text":"An uncaught error, from any realm (the error tap's records carry its file and line; a rejection says so; the\nworkbench logs its own as \"uncaught error\"): to the shell, which reports it with its sign-in, if any, and shows\nits id (shell/reporting.ts; packages/api/README.md O6).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:42.551Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:42.551Z"}
{"id":"c82846e3-9331-4ada-a213-574b6613dd70","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"aa091e66606e3865","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"a1334ab093a7b570a80cccf308b1c6e5be1faf7e","start":5930,"end":5969},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","tabRpc","=","createRpcClient","(","rootHub",")"]},"context":{"before":"c1852e768376b921","after":"25dde730b03dfa5e"}},"payload":{"text":"What the service worker relays for this tab (it serves every tab: `/__virtual__/<tab>/<port>/` names which) to its\ndev-server worker, below this root; and which tab this is, for an address (workbench/node-runner.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:39.711Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:39.711Z"}
{"id":"d7cbe308-5415-440e-a479-3e83e36e1682","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"77a462f283c979c6","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"93f3b06a4a44d6d4c53deac433b2df63b295b91b","start":2398,"end":2439},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","seeded","=","seedFiles","(","location",".","search",")"]},"context":{"before":"3fbc6400271695ab#2","after":"d65514566fc3605b"}},"payload":{"text":"The workbench opens on the bundled demo workspace (snapshot.ts bakes `demo/` in at build time as\n`editor:workspace`). The dependency type surface (`editor:types`) is seeded alongside so the\nin-browser TS server resolves the demo's imports, and `editor:versions` drives the CDN node_modules\noverlay for go-to-definition into real dependency source. A real on-disk folder (File System Access)\nbecomes an additional source mode later. Both load DYNAMICALLY: the type surface is ~480KB the shell (top\nlevel) never uses, and the app only needs them to answer the workbench's `workbench.init`, well after it\ncreates the workbench iframe — so neither is on the path to that.\n(an instance seeded by its address has those files in place of the starter: shared/instance.ts)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:48.297Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:48.297Z"}
{"id":"da854ff4-4df3-448e-9bbc-8714130ddc79","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"14adacc847206c58","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"c54341db392d0e75ed2a881ed9b8219186289201","start":8170,"end":8699},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","embedded",")","{","rootHub",".","link","(","windowTransport","(","window",".","parent",")",")",";","rootHub",".","subscribe","(","\"","project.openFiles","\"",",","(","data",")","=>","{","const","request","=","data","as","{","\"","files","\"","?",":","{","\"","path","\"",":","string",";","\"","contents","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","bytes","\"","?",":","Uint8Array","}","[]",";","\"","openEditors","\"","?",":","string","[]","}","|","null",";","if","(","Array",".","isArray","(","request","?.","files",")","&&","request",".","files",".","length",">","0",")","{","vscodeWindow",".","replaceProject","(","request",".","files",",","request",".","openEditors","??","[","]",")",";","hostLog",".","info","(","\"","project.openFiles","\"",",","{","\"","files","\"",":","request",".","files",".","length","}",")",";","}","}",")",";","hostLog",".","info","(","\"","shell link established","\"",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"9b33cc19805da7a0"}},"payload":{"text":"When embedded in the outer shell (shell.html), link the root hub UP to the shell over the window boundary\nand take the projects it loads. Standalone (top-level) load is unchanged — no parent to link, so none of this runs.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:33.786Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:33.786Z"}
{"id":"f4f10b7b-b26b-41db-9fa8-019e1c34dffc","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0279b6ae3cca3c36","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"d066aa34c97dfe1ecb6b1c902847e6cc334622d9","start":8466,"end":8483},"shape":{"type":"MemberExpression","atoms":["rootHub",".","subscribe"]},"context":{"before":"655a64535c76cf57","after":"1f68534cf2d876f5#0"}},"payload":{"text":"A GitHub repo loaded by the shell (which holds the token): the shell fetches the files and sends them here\n(files cross the boundary, the token never does), and we write them straight into the workspace. Binary\nfiles arrive as `bytes`; text as `contents`.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:32.383Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:32.383Z"}
{"id":"5071bbdf-f73c-4340-8ed2-93eae47c072a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6bbb3bd670093e52","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/main.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"b9a08532f9abcd65eb33c476443a1eab18ded15e","start":3564,"end":3585},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["linkDebugMcp","(","rootHub",")"]},"context":{"before":"e8a4d5a3723c0a8b","after":"205b9913e8c34b34"}},"payload":{"text":"dev-only: federate the tree to a running @brianjenkins94/debug-mcp for MCP querying","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T19:06:40.585Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T19:06:40.585Z"}
